## Step 1: Quality Control (FastQC + MultiQC)

### Commands

FastQC is a quality control tool that analyzes high-throughput sequencing data to generate a quick visual report containing potential issues, base quality scores, adapter contamination, or GC content.  
It evaluates raw sequencing quality for one sample at a time. 

Activate Conda prior to Fastqc
```
conda activate snps
```
Make a directory 01_fastqc
```
mkdir 01_fastqc
```
Select a file name and make a directory for the individual samples A-D and enter file.
```
mkdir Sample_A
cd Sample_A
```
When in the directory, start fastqc for each sample group. The -o flag specifies the output directory followed with a space and the directory ( . is the current directory).
```
fastqc ../../Raw_data/Sample_A_R1.fastq.gz -o . /
```


MultiQC gives a rounded number for total reads and does not report total bases per sample. To find out those numbers use this:

```
for f in *.fastq.gz; do
  echo -ne "$f\t"
  zcat "$f" | awk 'NR%4==2{r++; b+=length($0)} END{printf "%d\t%d\t%.1f\n", r, b, b/r}'
done | column -t
```

This gives the total reads, then the total bases, then the average read length for each file.

